  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieved 0.485 accuracy, while config_010 (image_only, resnet50) was very weak at 0.208, indicating RNA is the dominant signal. However, we have only tested one RNA encoder (PCA, a linear method). Question: Does a learned nonlinear representation (scvi_n200) substantially outperform PCA for the RNA modality? This experiment changes only the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 while keeping singleprofile and rna_only fixed, directly isolating the encoder effect against config_001. Why now: With 7 experiments remaining, establishing whether the RNA representation is a bottleneck is the highest-leverage uncertainty to resolve. If scvi_n200 significantly improves accuracy, it justifies investing remaining budget in scvi-based multimodal configs; if it does not, PCA is sufficient and we can pivot to profile-setting or fusion experiments without wasting budget on scvi/scgpt variants."
}

